ci(website): GitHub Actions workflow runs build:full + deploys snap to prod

CF Pages git integration can't run snap (no chromium in its
build image). This workflow takes the deploy:

  - runs on push to main affecting website-v2/**
  - installs chromium via playwright install
  - runs build:full (the existing build + snap-routes)
  - hard-fails if dist/<route>/index.html still has an empty root
    (defense in depth — refuses to deploy empty bodies)
  - deploys dist/ to the existing 'port-daddy' Cloudflare Pages
    project via wrangler-action

Concurrency-grouped so two pushes don't race. Manual
workflow_dispatch with a --branch input for previews.

Required secrets (operator action if not set yet):
  - CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN: Pages:Edit on the port-daddy project
  - CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID: from the Pages dashboard URL

The CF Pages git integration may still fire on the same push and
ship empty-body HTML first. This workflow runs afterward and
overwrites with snapped HTML — last-writer-wins outcome: full
content reaches Google.


